      "notes": "All five claims are appropriately tiered and the quoted evidence entails the claims as stated. The measurable claims draw on parliamentary committee evidence, Resolution Foundation, and policy text \u2014 all appropriate sources. The projected claim (E25) is correctly labelled. The 600-people-a-day figure (E13) comes from a source labelled as projection-adjacent ('potentially reducing...600 people a day currently leave paid work') but the claim itself only asserts the baseline fact, not the projection \u2014 acceptable. Advocacy sources (Carers UK) are used for supporting context but not as the sole basis for the direction verdict; the rationale explicitly flags this limitation. Direction 'improves' is well-supported: all distributional incidence falls on a bottom-concentrated group with no offsetting regressive element identified. Magnitude 'moderate' and confidence 'moderate' are appropriately caveated given unspecified funding levels. No tier blurring, lever leakage, party identity, or false balance issues detected."
